onfirms every duplicate has `request_class=bulk-refund` and no idempotency key. Single-refund API traffic in the same window includes idempotency keys and did not duplicate.\n\n## Highest-Confidence Follow-Up Action\n\nReject bulk-refund requests unless they include an idempotency key; remove the `legacy_batch_header` bypass before re-enabling the endpoint.\n\n## Unresolved Ambiguity\n\nWorker replay was an early symptom theory but is not supported as the primary trigger by final evidence. The lack of idempotency keys in bulk-refund requests remains the confirmed root cause.\n---\n{\n  \"ranked_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"Bulk-refund requests were accepted without idempotency keys\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"corpus/timeline/incident_timeline.md\", \"corpus/tickets/TICKET-8729.md\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"Idempotency guardrail was skipped due to legacy_batch_header bypass\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"corpus/timeline/incident_timeline.md\", \"corpus/remediation/notes.md\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"Worker replay theory is not supported by final evidence\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"corpus/tickets/TICKET-8721.md\", \"corpus/tickets/TICKET-8729.md\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolved_ambiguity\": \"Worker replay was an early symptom theory but is not supported as the primary trigger by final evidence\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
